     mmkknneettiidd [--qq] [--gg _g_r_o_u_p___f_i_l_e] [--pp _p_a_s_s_w_d___f_i_l_e] [--hh _h_o_s_t_s___f_i_l_e]
             [--nn _n_e_t_i_d___f_i_l_e] [--dd _d_o_m_a_i_n]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmkknneettiidd utility processes the contents of the group(5), passwd(5),
     hosts(5) and netid(5) files into the format used to generate the
     _n_e_t_i_d_._b_y_n_a_m_e NIS map.  This map is used to hold credential information
     for both users and hosts in an operating system independent format.

     The mmkknneettiidd utility checks for duplicate occurrences of netids and fil‐
     ters them out.

     The mmkknneettiidd utility prints its results on the standard output.  It is
     usually called only by _/_v_a_r_/_y_p_/_M_a_k_e_f_i_l_e when rebuilding the NIS maps.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
     The mmkknneettiidd utility supports the following options:

     --qq      Normally, mmkknneettiidd prints a warning message when it encounters a
             duplicate netid.  This flag turns on 'quiet' mode, allowing the
             warnings to be suppressed.  Other error messages may still be
             generated.

     --gg _g_r_o_u_p___f_i_l_e
             Specify the location of the group information file.  The com‐
             piled-in default is _/_e_t_c_/_g_r_o_u_p.

     --pp _p_a_s_s_w_d___f_i_l_e
             Specify the location of the passwd information file.  The com‐
             piled-in default is _/_e_t_c_/_p_a_s_s_w_d.

     --hh _h_o_s_t_s___f_i_l_e
             Specify the location of the hosts database file.  The compiled-in
             default is _/_e_t_c_/_h_o_s_t_s.

     --nn _n_e_t_i_d___f_i_l_e
             Specify the location of the netid information file.  The com‐
             piled-in default is _/_e_t_c_/_n_e_t_i_d.  Note that no error is generated
             if the netid database cannot be found.  The netid database is not
             likely to be present on most systems until Secure RPC support is
             added to FreeBSD.

     --dd _d_o_m_a_i_n
             By default, the mmkknneettiidd utility uses the system domainname when
             generating netid records.  If the system domainname is not set,
             the domain must be specified on the command line with the --dd
             flag.  If the domainname is set, the --dd flag may be used to over‐
             ride it.

FFIILLEESS
     /var/yp/Makefile  the Makefile that calls yypp__mmkkddbb and mmkknneettiidd to build
                       the NIS databases
     /etc/group        the default group database file
     /etc/passwd       the default passwd database file
     /etc/hosts        the default hosts database file
     /etc/netid        the default netid database file

